# Patterns that are specific to a text editor, IDE, operating system, or user
# environment are not added here. They should be added to your local gitignore
# file instead:
# https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/git-basics/ignoring-files#configuring-ignored-files-for-all-repositories-on-your-computer

# Build subdirectories.
/*build*
!/build-aux
!/build_msvc

*.pyc

# Only ignore unexpected patches
*.patch
!ci/test/*.patch
!contrib/guix/patches/*.patch
!depends/patches/**/*.patch

/CMakeUserPresets.json

# Previous releases
/releases

# cargo default target dir
target/

/guix-build-*

/ci/scratch/
# Favilla additions to the fork's .gitignore.
# The publish step appends this block to the Bitcoin Core tree's existing
# .gitignore at repo root (or applies it as-is if the root file is regenerated).
# Nothing here is optional: every entry is either key material, a credential,
# a datadir, or a build artifact that must never reach the public repo.

### Favilla secrets and private material — NEVER PUBLIC
hidden_files/
testnet-burn-key-*.json
*key*.json
*.pem
*.key
wallet.dat
*.wif
upstream-node.txt
*.env
favilla.conf
bitcoin.conf

### Favilla datadirs and chain state
.favilla/
btc-testnet4/
favilla-claim-*/
favilla_btcheaders.dat
testnet-feed/upstream/
testnet-feed/headers-*.hex
testnet-feed/headers-*.txt
testnet-feed/*.log
testnet-feed/upstream-*.json

### Operator scratch
testnet-claim-5b/
testnet-claim-5a/
*.log
state.json
poll*.log

### Build artifacts and caches
build/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dat
*.tmp
*~

### Ephemeral host config
/etc/favilla/
